  "summary": "A session takeover while frames are in flight on the old connection, with the single owner (--delivery-shards 0: the coordinator is the only producer and the only receipt consumer, and finish_close is one step; runtime.rs start_takeover, close, finish_close, pump_will_connects; net.rs ConnCore::stop and ConnCore::finish_task; owner.rs plan_frame_result): the old peer is cancelled and shut down before the new generation is bound, each of its accepted frames gets exactly one terminal result, a result ends only the generation it names, and nothing is written to a socket once its terminal reason is recorded or, for the old one, once the new generation is bound. A TLS connection defers the shutdown to its task, which sends close_notify first and reads the cancellation at the start of a turn only (net.rs Connection::close, net/tls.rs Task): its peer then stays in the table until the task has finished, and the same properties hold. Not modelled, and present with --delivery-shards K >= 1: a shard that writes to the old connection and reads the receipts of its writes, and the two waits of finish_close (the task finished, the shard detached the session). Not modelled either: the MQTT 5 DISCONNECT (MDisconnectQueue), frames the core fails without submitting them, writes that carry several frames (MTransportCredit).",
